3. FULL GOVERNMENT-GRADE PROPOSAL / TENDER SPECIFICATION

This is formatted in a professional government-procurement style.


---

Project Title

National Meteorological Digital Services Platform (NMDSP)

Purpose

To establish a secure, high-availability, national digital weather platform providing real-time observations, warnings, radar/satellite imagery, and model forecasts to the public, government, media, aviation, and emergency services.


---

Scope of Work

1. Core Components

1.1 Website & UX

WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility

Responsive mobile-first design

Multilingual capability (if needed)

Warning banners, iconography, hazard dashboards

Custom map viewer


1.2 Data Ingestion & Processing

METAR, SYNOP, AWS ingest

Radar network ingest & composite grid generation

Himawari-8 satellite ingest (HSD format → NetCDF → render)

Ocean buoys, river gauges, lightning networks

External models (ECMWF, ICON)

Internal access to national NWP (ACCESS)

Full metadata, QC checks, and versioning


1.3 APIs

REST + WebSocket

1-minute observations

5-minute radar

Forecast endpoints

Bulk downloads (CSV/GRIB2/NetCDF)


1.4 Map & Visualisation Platform

Radar + satellite layers

Wind vectors, streamlines

Rainfall accumulation

Temperature anomalies

Fire danger indices

Aviation layers: SIGMET, TAF, METAR, AIRMET

Custom tiling (XYZ, WMTS, MVT)


1.5 Warnings & Alerts

CAP (Common Alerting Protocol) compliant

Fire, flood, cyclone, storm, heatwave

SMS/email/Push optional

Integration with emergency services


1.6 Cloud, Security, and Reliability

99.99% SLA

Multi-region failover

Geo-redundant object storage

DDoS mitigation

Annual penetration testing

Role-based access control

Logging + audit trails

Full incident response plan



---

Deliverables

Live national weather website

Public API documentation

Complete data ingestion pipeline

Custom GIS & mapping engine

Warning dashboard

User training manuals

Source code + DevOps scripts



